(PRC-14 — source, target, fstype and options each accept a string literal,
 a text variable, or a buffer, including a format-string-built buffer.
 The mount itself fails with EPERM (unprivileged, see PRC-12), which is
 what this probe wants: it proves the four operands COMPILE and are
 evaluated in every form, and it prints the format-built buffer so the
 interpolation is visible rather than assumed.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-14.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the variable-and-buffer mount set the error flag
   size=8m
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
a text called 'the source' is "tmpfs".
a text called 'the target' is "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_operands".
a buffer called 'the filesystem type' is "tmpfs".
a number called megabytes is 8.
a buffer called 'the mount options' is "size={megabytes}m".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_operands".
Mount 'the source' at 'the target' with type 'the filesystem type' with options 'the mount options'.
On error print "the variable-and-buffer mount set the error flag".
print 'the mount options'.
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_operands".
